{"id":"the-recipe","name":"The recipe","chapter":"Four handed siteswaps","kind":"guide","page":33,"label":"32","jugglers":2,"objects":6,"timing":null,"pdf":"https://www.jugglingedge.com/pdf/highgate.pdf#page=33&view=FitH,742","passist":"https://passist.org/siteswap/9784266?jugglers=2","passist_candidate":"https://passist.org/siteswap/9784266?jugglers=2","passist_fork":null,"notations":[{"type":"hg-siteswap-in-text","value":"9784266"},{"type":"hg-siteswap-in-text","value":"5340"},{"type":"hg-siteswap-in-text","value":"222"}],"derived":{"kind":"global-4hss","value":"9784266","global":"97842669784266","confidence":"medium","matches_stated":null},"body":[{"t":"li","h":"Take any siteswap. I&#x27;m going to choose the six object pattern 9784266."},{"t":"li","h":"Subtract 4 from every number to give a derived siteswap. In my example the derived"},{"t":"p","h":"siteswap is 5340-222. (Despite the negative number, this is still theoretically a siteswap)!"},{"t":"li","h":"Number the beats in a causal diagram as follows:"},{"t":"d","i":0},{"t":"li","h":"Now for beat 1, add the first number in the derived siteswap: 5, and you get 1+5=6. So on"},{"t":"p","h":"the diagram draw a line from beat 1 to beat 6:"},{"t":"d","i":1},{"t":"li","h":"For beat 2, add the second number in the derived siteswap: 3, and you get 2+3=5. So on"},{"t":"p","h":"the diagram draw a line from beat 2 to beat 5:"},{"t":"d","i":2},{"t":"li","h":"For beat 3, add the third number in the derived siteswap: 4, and you get 3+4=7. So on the"},{"t":"p","h":"diagram draw a line from beat 3 to beat 7:"},{"t":"d","i":3},{"t":"li","h":"For beat 4, add the fourth number in the derived siteswap: 0, and you get 4+0=4. So on the"},{"t":"p","h":"diagram draw a line from beat 4 to beat 4 (or leave it out):"},{"t":"d","i":4},{"t":"li","h":"For beat 5, add the fifth number in the derived siteswap: -2, and you get 5-2=3. So on the"},{"t":"p","h":"diagram draw a line from beat 5 to beat 3:"},{"t":"d","i":5},{"t":"li","h":"For beat 6, add the sixth number in the derived siteswap: 2, you get 6+2=8. So on the"},{"t":"p","h":"diagram draw a line from beat 6 to beat 8:"},{"t":"d","i":6},{"t":"li","h":"For beat 7, add the seventh number in the derived siteswap: 2, you get 7+2=9. So on the"},{"t":"p","h":"diagram draw a line from beat 7 to beat 9:"},{"t":"d","i":7},{"t":"li","h":"As there is no eighth number in the derived siteswap, for beat 8, we return to the beginning"},{"t":"p","h":"of the derived siteswap. When you add the first number: 5, you get 8+5=13. So on the diagram draw a line from beat 8 to beat 13:"},{"t":"d","i":8},{"t":"li","h":"If you apply the same procedure for all the remaining beats you end up with the following"},{"t":"p","h":"pattern:"},{"t":"d","i":9},{"t":"p","h":"This is a six club pattern, which is good because we started with a six object siteswap!"},{"t":"p","h":"Both jugglers start with two clubs in their right hand and one club in their left hand. Anne&#x27;s pattern is: double heff zip self pass hold self. Anne&#x27;s double passes cross and her single passes are straight. Ben starts slightly after Anne. His pattern is: pass hold self double heff zip self. Ben&#x27;s double passes are straight and his single passes cross."},{"t":"p","h":"The following table shows all the throws in four handed siteswap up to height b (11)."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"hr"}],"drawings":[{"file":"p33-1.png","kind":"causal diagram","reading":{"rows":[{"juggler":"A","name":"Anne","offset":0.0,"tempo":1.0,"beats":[{"t":0.0,"hand":"R","n":1},{"t":1.0,"hand":"L","n":3},{"t":2.0,"hand":"R","n":5},{"t":3.0,"hand":"L","n":7},{"t":4.0,"hand":"R","n":9},{"t":5.0,"hand":"L","n":11},{"t":6.0,"hand":"R","n":13},{"t":7.0,"hand":"L","n":15},{"t":8.0,"hand":"R","n":17},{"t":9.0,"hand":"L","n":19},{"t":10.0,"hand":"R","n":21},{"t":11.0,"hand":"L","n":23},{"t":12.0,"hand":"R","n":25},{"t":13.0,"hand":"L","n":27},{"t":14.0,"hand":"R","n":29}]},{"juggler":"B",